# Divya Laxmi Edamakanti — Portfolio Website

A cinematic, fully responsive personal portfolio website built with pure HTML, CSS, and vanilla JavaScript. Features premium dark-mode aesthetics, smooth animations, and an interactive UI designed to showcase web development skills.

---

## ✨ Features

- **Cinematic Hero Section** — Floating profile image with film-frame corners, scan-line effect, ambient glow orbs, and a live "Available" status badge
- **Typing Effect** — Animated role titles cycling through Web Developer, Frontend Engineer, Python Developer, UI/UX Enthusiast
- **Custom Cursor** — Dual-layer magnetic cursor with blend-mode effect (desktop only)
- **Scroll Progress Bar** — Thin gradient bar at the top tracking scroll position
- **Scroll Reveal Animations** — Elements fade up into view as the user scrolls
- **Animated Skill Bars** — Progress bars that fill when scrolled into view
- **Interactive Timeline** — Pulsing dot timeline for Education and Experience
- **Project Cards** — Hover zoom on thumbnails, supports both image and video previews
- **Self-Introduction Video** — Embedded video section with cinematic overlay
- **Certifications Grid** — Decorative accent cards for internships and credentials
- **Contact Form** — Client-side form with animated submit feedback
- **Embedded Google Map** — Location pin for Ongole, Andhra Pradesh
- **Sticky Navigation** — Active link highlighting based on scroll position, mobile hamburger menu
- **Footer** — Social links with back-to-top button
- **Noise Texture Overlay** — Subtle cinematic film grain on the background
- **Fully Responsive** — Tested across desktop (1280px+), tablet (768px), and mobile (480px)
- **Accessibility** — `prefers-reduced-motion` respected, ARIA labels on icon-only buttons

---

## 🗂️ File Structure

```
portfolio/
├── index.html       ← Single-file portfolio (HTML + CSS + JS)
└── README.md        ← This file
```

All styles and scripts are inlined in `index.html` — no build step or dependencies required beyond CDN fonts and Font Awesome icons.

---

## 🚀 Getting Started

### Run Locally

1. Download or clone the repository
2. Open `index.html` in any modern browser

```bash
# No installation needed — just open the file
open index.html
```

### Deploy to GitHub Pages

1. Push the project to a GitHub repository
2. Go to **Settings → Pages**
3. Set source to the `main` branch, root folder
4. Your portfolio will be live at `https://<username>.github.io/<repo-name>/`

### Deploy to Netlify

Drag and drop the project folder onto [netlify.com/drop](https://app.netlify.com/drop) — live in seconds.

